1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,743
Every campaign begins with choices.

2
00:00:02,743 --> 00:00:05,314
Which creators belong in the plan?

3
00:00:05,314 --> 00:00:07,029
What will they cost?

4
00:00:07,029 --> 00:00:15,171
Creator Campaign Contribution Planner brings the available
numbers together, helping growth teams compare their options
before committing a budget.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,743
Start with the campaign overview.

6
00:00:20,743 --> 00:00:25,886
See the recommended combination, estimated profit, creator fees,
and remaining budget together.

7
00:00:25,886 --> 00:00:32,314
The summary follows your selected creators, so you can
understand the plan as a whole.

8
00:00:32,314 --> 00:00:34,029
These figures are illustrative.

9
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:40,029
When the list grows, focus on what matters.

10
00:00:40,029 --> 00:00:46,029
Search for a creator by name, or choose a category to narrow the
table.

11
00:00:46,029 --> 00:00:51,171
Compare the visible orders, discounts, costs, and fees before
looking more closely.

12
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,171
A recommendation is a starting point.

13
00:00:57,171 --> 00:01:01,029
Select or remove creators to explore a different combination.

14
00:01:01,029 --> 00:01:05,314
The summary updates with your choices, showing the remaining
budget.

15
00:01:05,314 --> 00:01:09,600
If the plan exceeds it, a warning makes that visible.

16
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:13,886
Open the calculator.

17
00:01:13,886 --> 00:01:18,171
Set your budget, category, and minimum and maximum creator
count.

18
00:01:18,171 --> 00:01:22,886
It searches combinations for the highest estimated profit within
those limits.

19
00:01:22,886 --> 00:01:27,600
Aggregate estimates do not yet adjust for returns or attribution
overlap.

20
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:35,314
Open a creator profile to see the person behind a row.

21
00:01:35,314 --> 00:01:40,029
Review their identity and platform audience figures alongside
their campaign details.

22
00:01:40,029 --> 00:01:46,029
Here, the creator information and audience numbers come from the
project’s illustrative sample data.

23
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,029
The coupon code stays close to the creator.

24
00:01:52,029 --> 00:01:57,600
Edit it directly in the profile; spaces are removed and letters
become capitals.

25
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:00,600
The change is saved in this browser.

26
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,029
It does not create a live merchant coupon.

27
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,029
Move from a campaign total to individual orders.

28
00:02:10,029 --> 00:02:13,457
Review each sample customer identifier, product, and price.

29
00:02:13,457 --> 00:02:21,600
Delivered, shipped, and returned statuses sit beside the
records, making it easier to inspect what the displayed activity
contains.

30
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,600
Creator fees are part of the economics.

31
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:34,457
The product table allocates the creator fee across attributed
orders, showing an influencer cost per product.

32
00:02:34,457 --> 00:02:39,600
Use this view to understand that allocation alongside the
displayed product prices.

33
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,171
The profile brings customer signals together.

34
00:02:45,171 --> 00:02:52,029
Review returns, average order value, repeat customers, and
estimated net profit for the illustrative order sample.

35
00:02:52,029 --> 00:02:57,600
These profile figures describe that sample, separately from the
campaign’s aggregate order counts.

36
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,743
Discovery begins with a question.

37
00:03:02,743 --> 00:03:09,600
On YouTube, enter a keyword and choose a country to find
channels through the official interface.

38
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,171
Server access must be configured first.

39
00:03:12,171 --> 00:03:16,029
Live discovery has not been verified in this demonstration.

40
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:20,743
Instagram follows a different path.

41
00:03:20,743 --> 00:03:27,600
Enter known usernames for business or creator accounts, then
look them up through the official interface.

42
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,743
Account access must be configured.

43
00:03:29,743 --> 00:03:33,600
This feature does not provide keyword search across Instagram.

44
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:40,457
Refine the discovery results by follower range and niche.

45
00:03:40,457 --> 00:03:45,171
The largest audiences appear first, making the list easier to
compare.

46
00:03:45,171 --> 00:03:52,029
Niche is inferred from public text; the examples shown here are
illustrative, rather than live results.

47
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:58,886
Keep promising creators on a shortlist saved in this browser.

48
00:03:58,886 --> 00:04:04,029
Add an account from the results, or remove it when priorities
change.

49
00:04:04,029 --> 00:04:09,600
Stored entries expire after thirty days, helping the shortlist
remain a working selection.

50
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,314
Creator Campaign Contribution Planner.

51
00:04:14,314 --> 00:04:19,886
Explore the creators, understand the assumptions, and compare
the options within your budget.

52
00:04:19,886 --> 00:04:23,743
A clearer view supports a more considered next decision.

53
00:04:23,743 --> 00:04:27,600
The demonstration uses sample data, not verified commercial
results.
